  "summary": "John Paul McQueen and Craig Dean—known to fans as “McDean”—are a popular couple from *Hollyoaks*. Their relationship developed from a close friendship into a secret romance in 2007, attracting a large fan following and praise from LGBT rights groups.\n\nCraig, initially portrayed as heterosexual, struggled to understand his feelings for John Paul while dating Sarah Barnes. John Paul, who was coming to terms with being gay, fell in love with Craig. Their affair continued alongside Craig’s relationship with Sarah, causing jealousy, deception and conflict. The affair was exposed at Craig and Sarah’s engagement party when Sarah found the two men kissing. Craig then left for college in Dublin, while John Paul remained in Hollyoaks.\n\nThe actors described the storyline differently: Guy Burnet said he wanted viewers to remain uncertain about Craig’s sexuality, while James Sutton was comfortable portraying John Paul. Both praised their working relationship. Burnet left the show in 2007, and Sutton departed in 2008. Burnet returned for the characters’ reunion, which gave John Paul and Craig a happy “sunset ending” before both actors left the series.",
